Example rules for a different gridworld (not this one), in priority order:
```
{"condition": "x = 1 & y = 4", "action": "left"}
{"condition": "!g1 & x = 2 & y < 3", "action": "right"}
{"condition": "!g1 & y = 3", "action": "down"}
{"condition": "g1 & !g2 & x > 0", "action": "up"}
{"condition": "true", "action": "down"}
```
Rule 1 is a one-cell exception, so it comes before the general rules that also match that cell. Rule 2 moves right along row 2 before goal 1, rule 3 then goes down column 3, rule 4 heads up after goal 1, and the last rule is a catch-all default that covers every remaining state.
